r with a big reveal and because players are bad about accidentally sharing info they shouldn't. I can easily believe that the Empress would be able to recognize that one of the player characters is a liability in that regard.</li> <li>This story works best for solars, dragon-blooded, or lunars in my estimation. If you don't want that to happen, or are running a different faction, you can have her be an odd advisor to Roseblack (see below).</li> </ul></li> <li>When she sees that the world is at a tipping point, she disappears, just like in the core timeline.<ul><li>She knows that she's going to be a target by the deathlords and every other faction including some of the nascent solars that she would like to ally with.</li> <li>If she helps fight against these threats, and wins, then she'll be even more of linchpin then before, which means that the world is even more dependent on her and a system that she feels trapped by.</li> <li>She knows that if things do go super wrong, that she has the Imperial Manse in her back pocket.</li> </ul></li> <li>Scarlet Empress then goes to advise the PCs and/or the Roseblack on things as the classic mysterious mentor.<ul><li>This will make the players feel special. Players love when cool npcs say that their characters are cool.</li> <li>She can serve as a way for the storyteller to give information that there's really not a good way for the players to know it.<ul><li>An easy way to do this is, instead of the answer, the Empress gives information that allows the players to find the answer, such as a lost manse, or a secret unguarded passage that leads to the Underworld. This includes even information on how to possibly break the Great Curse. She probably doesn't know about that, but has suspicions like you see a few sidereals have, and then that allows the players an in-character path to trying to fix the world.</li> <li>Why not give the information or fight the fights? Besides the fact that it might overshadow the PCs, especially if they're dragon-blooded, is that she's trying to not be a linchpin anymore. Flavor-wise, the helps reconnect all the strands of fate that are bound into her back into the world.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul>What are people's thoughts?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, I think this would make a great story, it makes her feel less mustachio twirling and more just someone trying to navigate things the best she can and trying to setup a way to break free of the political machine she had to build to keep everything from destroying itself. Hell, I could see a story where she is even still &quot;working&quot; with ED so she can get access to a group of Infernals that she is deprogramming from the Yozi brain washing and trying to be a somewhat force of good on creation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T14:42:34-07:00","id":1524370,"title":"","content":"I like it, and over the years have seen similar ideas posted. I think if you look up &quot;what are your head canon&quot; type of threads on here, reddit, or other forums you can find other ideas for the disappearance of the empress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}